  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 0. Setup\n\nEverything is a function of the twists (z, w); no globals zN/wN. Generators JJ are plain (exact rationals, non-Hermitian); the invariant inner product is G = diag(...) so P_HW is the G-orthogonal projector. Point A: v2 = e1 rho(n_A), v1 = e1 (1 + beta E12 + gamma (E13 + E12 E23/2)) rho(n_A) rho(Delta) with the exact closed-form beta, gamma; undo phi_A = v1 rho(n_A)^-1. First a finite-twist regression test, then the small-eps regime.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* fresh kernel state; this also clears the other new-conventions notebooks' session state (their files are untouched); Quiet because the front-end wrapper symbol ClearGlobals is Protected *)\nQuiet[ClearAll[\"Global`*\"]];\n(* GT basis and gl(3) generators, verbatim from L2-310-two-rotations.wb (plain, non-Hermitian, exact rationals) *)\nps[rep_] := ps[rep] = Block[{res = (Prepend[rep, #1] &) /@ Tuples[Table[Range[rep[[1, i + 1]], rep[[1, i]]], {i, 1, Length[rep[[1]]] - 1}]]}, If[Length[res[[1, 1]]] == 1, Reverse[Sort[res]], Reverse[Sort[Flatten[ps /@ res, 1]]]]];\ndim[rep_] := dim[rep] = Length[ps[{rep}]];\nJ0[k_][pat_] := J0[k][pat] = Sum[pat[[k, i]], {i, 1, k}] - Sum[pat[[k - 1, i]], {i, 1, k - 1}];\nJp[k_][pat_] := Jp[k][pat] = -Sum[(Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k + 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k + 1]}]/Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}])*v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] + 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nJm[k_][pat_] := Jm[k][pat] = Sum[(Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k - 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k - 1]}]/Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}])*v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] - 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nJJ[k_, l_, rep_] := JJ[k, l, rep] = Which[\n  k == l, DiagonalMatrix[J0[k] /@ ps[{rep}]],\n  l == k + 1, Transpose[Table[(Coefficient[Jp[k][ps[{rep}][[i]]], v[#1]] &) /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]],\n  l == k - 1, Transpose[Table[(Coefficient[Jm[l][ps[{rep}][[i]]], v[#1]] &) /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]],\n  l > k + 1, JJ[k, k + 1, rep] . JJ[k + 1, l, rep] - JJ[k + 1, l, rep] . JJ[k, k + 1, rep],\n  l < k - 1, JJ[k, k - 1, rep] . JJ[k - 1, l, rep] - JJ[k - 1, l, rep] . JJ[k, k - 1, rep]];\nchecks = <||>;\n(* size of a residual: a numerically exact zero (tracked-precision zero) is reported by its accuracy bound 10^-Accuracy, so it is never mistaken for an exact 0 (Clean-CG-combinations trap) *)\nshowChecks[pre_] := Grid[List @@@ Select[Normal[checks], StringStartsQ[#[[1]], Alternatives @@ pre] &], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left];\nsz[x_] := If[x == 0, 10.^-Accuracy[x], N[Abs[x], 3]];\npr = 200; Λ = {3, 1, 0}; nL = 2; d1 = dim[Λ]; d2 = d1^nL;\nhN = 1/2; thN = {2/7, -3/5};\nid1 = IdentityMatrix[d1, SparseArray]; id2 = IdentityMatrix[d2, SparseArray];\nEe[i_, j_] := Ee[i, j] = SparseArray[JJ[i, j, Λ]];\nE1[i_, j_] := E1[i, j] = KroneckerProduct[Ee[i, j], id1];\nE2[i_, j_] := E2[i, j] = KroneckerProduct[id1, Ee[i, j]];\n(* total gl(3) weight of each product basis state, in KroneckerProduct order *)\nwtBasis = Flatten[Table[Table[J0[k][p1] + J0[k][p2], {k, 3}], {p1, ps[{Λ}]}, {p2, ps[{Λ}]}], 1];\nsecOf[mu_] := secOf[mu] = Flatten[Position[wtBasis, mu]];\n(* gl(3) commutation relations of JJ (exact) *)\ncomm = Flatten[Table[Normal[Ee[i, j] . Ee[k, l] - Ee[k, l] . Ee[i, j] - (KroneckerDelta[j, k] Ee[i, l] - KroneckerDelta[l, i] Ee[k, j])], {i, 3}, {j, 3}, {k, 3}, {l, 3}]];\nchecks[\"JJ gl(3) relations\"] = Union[comm] === {0};\n(* invariant diagonal metric G (G[[1]] = 1): Ee[i,j]^T G = G Ee[j,i]. JJ is not Hermitian, so projectors must be G-orthogonal (= orthogonal in the Hermitian EH frame) *)\ngv = Array[gg, d1];\ngsol = Solve[Flatten[Append[Table[Transpose[Normal[Ee[i, j]]] . DiagonalMatrix[gv] - DiagonalMatrix[gv] . Normal[Ee[j, i]], {i, 3}, {j, i + 1, 3}], {gv[[1]] - 1}]] == 0, gv];\ngMet = DiagonalMatrix[gv /. First[gsol]];\nchecks[\"G unique, positive, invariant for all Ee[i,j]\"] = Length[gsol] === 1 && And @@ Positive[Diagonal[gMet]] && And @@ Flatten[Table[Transpose[Normal[Ee[i, j]]] . gMet === gMet . Normal[Ee[j, i]], {i, 3}, {j, 3}]];\nchecks[\"nilpotency Ee[i,j]^4 = 0 (i != j), Ee[1,3]^3 != 0\"] = And @@ Flatten[Table[If[i == j, True, Max[Abs[Normal[MatrixPower[Ee[i, j], 4]]]] == 0, True], {i, 3}, {j, 3}]] && Max[Abs[Normal[MatrixPower[Ee[1, 3], 3]]]] != 0;\nGrid[Join[{{\"Λ, d1, d2\", ToString[{Λ, d1, d2}]}, {\"distinct total weights\", Length[Union[wtBasis]]}, {\"diag G\", ToString[Diagonal[gMet]]}, {\"pr\", pr}}, List @@@ Normal[checks]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "Output of the cell above (kernel K1, cell source run via Get; VS Code did not execute this new file):\n\n```\n{\"Λ, d1, d2\", \"{{3, 1, 0}, 15, 225}\"}\n{\"distinct total weights\", 36}\n{\"diag G\", \"{1, 1, 2, 3, 24, 32, 4, 12, 24, 64, 288, 576, 36, 128, 576}\"}\n{\"pr\", 200}\n{\"JJ gl(3) relations\", True}\n{\"G unique, positive, invariant for all Ee[i,j]\", True}\n{\"nilpotency Ee[i,j]^4 = 0 (i != j), Ee[1,3]^3 != 0\", True}\n```",
   "languageId": "markdown",
