  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* eigenstates of one total-weight sector mu at the ket twist zz (exact rational list in, numeric pr inside), normalized <x0|Psi> = 1; each state carries its transfer eigenvalue polynomials t1,t2 (read off at the largest component; coefficients above the true degrees 2a are dropped and the dropped size is reported), t3 = quantum determinant, its dual Q's (degrees mu_j), the exact-arithmetic Baxter residual, the raising residual rr = ||(E12+E12, E23+E23) Psi||/||Psi|| (rr ~ 0 marks the HW-limit states), and for the HW sectors ||P_HW Psi||/||Psi|| in the invariant G-norm. Memoized on (zz, mu): purge with literal symbols only (cell 'purge'). *)\nraiseSec[mu_] := raiseSec[mu] = With[{sec = secOf[mu]}, Normal[Join[(E1[1, 2] + E2[1, 2])[[All, sec]], (E1[2, 3] + E2[2, 3])[[All, sec]]]]];\nstatesCore[zz_, mu_] := statesCore[zz, mu] = Module[{zn = N[zz, pr], tc, x0, sec = secOf[mu], mix, es, rr, isHW = MemberQ[hwSecs, mu], out = {}},\n  tc = tZof[zn]; x0 = x0Of[zn];\n  mix = Normal[(tEval[tc, 1, 3/7] + N[Pi, pr] tEval[tc, 2, 3/7])[[sec, sec]]];\n  es = Eigensystem[mix];\n  rr = Table[Norm[raiseSec[mu] . v]/Norm[v], {v, es[[2]]}];\n  Do[Module[{psiS, psi, km, tt, qq, st, dropped},\n    psiS = es[[2, k]]/(x0[[sec]] . es[[2, k]]);\n    psi = Normal[SparseArray[Thread[sec -> psiS], {d2}]];\n    km = First@Ordering[Abs[psiS], -1];\n    tt = Table[Sum[u^(j - 1) ((tc[[a, j]][[sec, sec]] . psiS)[[km]]/psiS[[km]]), {j, 1 + 2 a}], {a, 2}];\n    dropped = Max[Table[Abs[(tc[[a, j]][[sec, sec]] . psiS)[[km]]/psiS[[km]]], {a, 2}, {j, 2 a + 2, 7}]];\n    tt = Append[tt, auditQdet[zn, hN, thN, u]];\n    qq = Table[auditMonicQ[tt, zn[[j]], 1, mu[[j]], hN, thN, pr], {j, 3}];\n    st = <|\"qu\" -> qq, \"z\" -> zn|>;\n    AppendTo[out, <|\"mu\" -> mu, \"k\" -> k, \"psi\" -> psi, \"ev\" -> es[[1, k]], \"rr\" -> rr[[k]], \"tt\" -> tt, \"qu\" -> qq, \"st\" -> st, \"bax\" -> baxRes[tt, qq, zn, 1], \"dropped\" -> dropped, \"x0ov\" -> (x0[[sec]] . es[[2, k]]), \"hwFrac\" -> If[isHW, gNorm[PHWc[mu][psi]]/gNorm[psi], Indeterminate]|>]], {k, Length[sec]}];\n  out];\n(* all states of the 8 HW sectors at zz; HW-limit branches = the dim(HW_mu) states of each sector with the smallest rr, copies ordered by Re of the eigenvalue of t1 + Pi t2 at u = 3/7 *)\nbranchesAt[zz_] := branchesAt[zz] = Module[{out = {}},\n  Do[Module[{ss = statesCore[zz, mu], nHW = Length[hwKets[mu]], pick},\n    pick = SortBy[Ordering[ss[[All, \"rr\"]], nHW], Re[ss[[#, \"ev\"]]] &];\n    Do[AppendTo[out, Append[ss[[k]], <|\"branch\" -> MemberQ[pick, k], \"copy\" -> If[MemberQ[pick, k], Position[pick, k][[1, 1]], 0]|>]], {k, Length[ss]}]], {mu, hwSecs}];\n  <|\"states\" -> out, \"zz\" -> zz|>];\nbrOf[B_, mu_, copy_] := First@Select[B[\"states\"], #[\"mu\"] === mu && #[\"copy\"] === copy &];\nbrList[B_] := brOf[B, #[[1]], #[[2]]] & /@ hwList;\n(* purge of every memoized point-dependent definition, LITERAL symbols only (DownValues is HoldAll: a Do over a symbol list purges nothing, adjoint cell 36) *)\npurge[] := (DownValues[Tm] = Select[DownValues[Tm], ! FreeQ[#[[1]], Pattern] &]; DownValues[tBasisC] = Select[DownValues[tBasisC], ! FreeQ[#[[1]], Pattern] &]; DownValues[tBasisN] = Select[DownValues[tBasisN], ! FreeQ[#[[1]], Pattern] &]; DownValues[tZof] = Select[DownValues[tZof], ! FreeQ[#[[1]], Pattern] &]; DownValues[wgt] = Select[DownValues[wgt], ! FreeQ[#[[1]], Pattern] &]; DownValues[statesCore] = Select[DownValues[statesCore], ! FreeQ[#[[1]], Pattern] &]; DownValues[branchesAt] = Select[DownValues[branchesAt], ! FreeQ[#[[1]], Pattern] &]; DownValues[raiseSec] = Select[DownValues[raiseSec], ! FreeQ[#[[1]], Pattern] &];);\n(* time one sector (the largest, (3,3,2), 18 states) at a regime point *)\nzTest = reg[10^-6, phiP, 3/4, -1/5][\"z\"];\n{tSec, ss332} = AbsoluteTiming[statesCore[zTest, {3, 3, 2}]];\nGrid[{{\"time (s), sector (3,3,2) (18 states), eps = 1e-6\", tSec}, {\"# states\", Length[ss332]}, {\"max exact Baxter residual (dual Q's)\", ScientificForm[Max[ss332[[All, \"bax\"]]], 3]}, {\"max dropped high coefficients of t1,t2\", ScientificForm[sz[Max[ss332[[All, \"dropped\"]]]], 3]}, {\"sorted rr (smallest 4, then next)\", ToString[N[Sort[ss332[[All, \"rr\"]]][[1 ;; 5]], 3]]}, {\"min |<x0|psi_unnormalized>|\", ScientificForm[Min[Abs[ss332[[All, \"x0ov\"]]]], 3]}, {\"Precision of psi\", Min[Precision /@ ss332[[All, \"psi\"]]]}}, Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "Output of the cell above (kernel K1, cell source run via Get; VS Code did not execute this new file):\n\n```\n{\"time (s), sector (3,3,2) (18 states), eps = 1e-6\", 1.3981285}\n{\"# states\", 18}\n{\"max exact Baxter residual (dual Q's)\", ScientificForm[2.376450659606454307217487103745147`6.*^-140, 3]}\n{\"max dropped high coefficients of t1,t2\", ScientificForm[0, 3]}\n{\"sorted rr (smallest 4, then next)\", \"        -7\\n{6.36 10  , 1.67, 1.83, 2.49, 2.92}\"}\n{\"min |<x0|psi_unnormalized>|\", ScientificForm[7.2675603697143466347663081346094518344432081388727756779201377716368462525237447366242904477894947088\\\n665851532613606929346892734908325258123094000942818042542380527`154.85883026263588*^-48, 3]}\n{\"Precision of psi\", 154.85883026263588}\n```",
