  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Finite-twist regression (z = (3/2,5/4,2/3), w = (5/2,7/3,3/5), y_A = -63/8): PASSED.** (i) <v1 (x) v2|HW> = s <phi_A (x) e1|HW> exactly on the 10 HW kets (s = 1). (ii) <v1 (x) v2|Psi>/<x0|Psi> = const x det6[Q_B, Q_vac(w)]/Psi_Q x det2^(0,1,2)[Q_B; y_A]/W(3,4) over **all 225 states** (36 weight sectors, 200 digits): max |ratio/ratio_1 - 1| = 1.3e-179 (Precision of the constant 187); controls fail (y = 2: 10.3, y = 3: 44.1, pole set {0..3} at y_A: 44.9). Max exact Baxter residual of the 225 dual Q's 3.8e-184; vacuum Q degrees (0,4,6), residual 5.3e-195. Timings: 225 states 13.4 s, det6 x det2 for 225 states 3.7 s, one R_Q 0.014 s. The closed forms as given in the spec are right: K12 = beta (w2-z1)/w2 = 2/25 and K13 = gamma (w2-z1)(y_A-z3)/w2^2 = **-189/704** (the notes quote +189/704: a sign typo in the notes; the formula of the spec passes the test).\n",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
