  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Round 2, Task A result (t-scan, h = 1, theta = (t,0), phi = phiP, om1 = 3/4, six om2, 3-eps Richardson; 20 t; fits on 14, held-out t = indices 3,6,9,12,15,18 of the list).** Sanity: at t = 62/35 (h = 1) the round-1 constants are reproduced (kappa = 1.385714286, 1.410569929, 0.986713486, 1.366101695, 4.650803571; slopes -1.9010706556, 0.9735128998; R = -0.8921886416, 1.2040698297). Memoized objects purged with literal symbols at every t. Time 30 s per t.\n\nExact untwisted data (rational, all 20 t, held-out exact): t2(theta1+h) on HW_[4,3,1]: tr = 8t^2+16t-8, det = 16 t (t-1)(t+1)(t+4); on HW_[5,2,1]: tr = 8t^2+19t-8, det = 4 (t+4)(t-1)(t+1)(4t+3) (h = 1; tau_c = eigenvalue/h^4, t = theta12/h). The copy eigenvalues of the branches' own t2 polynomials agree with these to 9e-19. **t1(theta1+h) is degenerate on the [4,3,1] pair (difference 4e-18)**, so the affine-in-t1 alternative cannot separate the copies (not tried further).\n\n(a) F0 = 0 branches, kappa = R_C/S = 1 + K/S (closed forms, residual max over the 14 fit / 6 held-out t):\n- [4,4,0]: kappa = (t+1)/2 (1.4e-18 / 2.6e-18) - the guess is right.\n- [4,2,2]: kappa = (11t-31)/(5(3t-7)) (3.4e-15 / 1.9e-17), with a POLE at t = 7/3 (the chain value there is -2.5e6, regulated by eps; that point is skipped). I.e. the leading covector coefficient vanishes at t = 7/3.\n- [3,3,2]: kappa = (t+1)(19t-49)/(40(t-2)) (7.2e-17 / 4.9e-17).\n- [4,3,1] pair: **kappa_c = A(t) + B(t) tau_c fits** with A = (-7t^4+26t^3-166t+75)/(9D), B = (7t^2-22t+23)/(36D), D = t^3+3t^2-17t+5 (fit set 3.0e-10 (near D's root t ~ 2.65 the data amplify), held-out 9.1e-16). Equivalent symmetric forms: kappa_a + kappa_b and kappa_a kappa_b are rational (deg 3/3) with the same denominator D (fits 2.5e-13, 2.8e-12 held-out).\n\n(b) [5,2,1] pair (copies sorted by tau, h = 1): the Q-side F0 spread <= 3.0e-15, line residual <= 1.3e-9 (worst at t = 29/15, close to the t = 2 singularity of y0).\n- Exact signal slopes: p1' = (t-5)/4, q1' = (7-3t)/2 (verified at all 20 t; at P1 59/70).\n- R_c (chain) = 3/2 - 2t + tau_c/(2(t+4)) (residual 1e-18; R_a + R_b = (16-7t)/(2(t+4)), R_a R_b = -7t/(2(t+4))).\n- slope_c = p1' + q1' R_c + Delta_c with **Delta_c = (111+44t-92t^2)/105 + (23t-13)/(105(t+4)) tau_c** (affine in tau_c; residual of the final formula on the slopes 7.1e-10 fit set / 1.6e-9 held-out, limited by the 1e-9 noise of the slopes, worst near t = 2). The coordinator's combination Delta'_c = slope_c + (t-2) R_c also is affine in tau_c: Delta'_c = (216 - 647t/2 + 13t^2)/105 + (263-13t)/(420(t+4)) tau_c, with the same residuals; note the signal's coefficient of R_c here is q1' = (7-3t)/2, not -(t-2), so Delta (the first) is the one that removes the signal. The coefficients with the common 1/105 are rationalized from a 1e-8-accurate least-squares fit; they are not exact-proven.\n- Delta_1 + Delta_2 = (-3t^2 + 143t/105 + 992/105)/(t+4) and the product: rational fits (2,1), (3,1) with held-out 5.6e-11, 1.5e-9 (coefficients only 1e-8-accurate).\n- Cross-check with round 1 (t = 62/35): the closed form gives Delta = 0.7655 for tau = 37.479 and -0.3419 for tau = 13.282 (round 1: 0.76580, -0.34194; residual within the quoted 1e-9 noise after rounding of the coefficients).\n\nWhat did NOT fit: (i) q1'(t) was reported as \"NO FIT\" by the automatic rational fit only because it vanishes at t = 7/3 (relative error 0/0); the linear form (7-3t)/2 is exact. (ii) affine-in-t1 for [4,3,1] is not testable (degenerate). (iii) Delta1+Delta2, Delta1 Delta2 and the A, B coefficients of Delta_c are noise-limited (1e-8) rational guesses.\n",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task A driver (run in the kernel, 20 t x ~30 s = 9 min; stored in tScanA): *)\ntList20 = {29/15, 5/2, 3/2, 7/3, 11/4, 13/5, 9/4, 17/6, 19/7, 8/3, 12/5, 7/2, 23/8, 16/5, 11/3, 14/5, 25/9, 13/4, 9/5, 21/8};\n{tScanTime, tScanA} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[scanT[t], {t, tList20}]]; setPoint[1/2, {2/7, -3/5}];",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
