  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Round 2, Task C result: pure Q-side extraction of all 10 HW branches.** Inputs from the Q side only: Qnum^tk = Qnum - Tq (Tq = top-kill det6 with the (w1,y_A)-vacuum) at 6 om2 x 4 eps; tau_c = t2(theta1+h)/h^4 from the dual-Q dictionary t2(theta1+h) = chi3 nu1(theta1+h) nu2(theta1) Q^j(theta1-h)/Q^j(theta1) (single-ratio form, Richardson in eps; agrees with the exact untwisted eigenvalues of Task A to 1e-18); the closed forms of Tasks A-B (kappa(t[, tau]); Delta_c for [5,2,1]; kslope for [4,3,1] and [4,2,2], fitted forms, labeled); exact covector functions (fac_k, xU, a-, b-slopes are analytic in the twists). The chain side enters only the comparison columns. Extraction: first direction u'.C = Qnum^tk/(delta^Lambda eps^k fac_k kappa) (k = leading covector order 0/1/2); second direction (dim-2 weights): R^Q from the om2-slope of F1/F0 minus the known signal and the closed-form remainder; the full slice from {u.C = R c1, u'.C = c1}. Closed forms were used everywhere, no \"measured constant\" was needed (the [4,3,1] alpha(t) and the Delta_c, kslope forms are fits with 1e-9..1e-11 noise).\n\n**P1 (h = 1/2, theta = (2/7,-3/5), t = 62/35)** (err = max over 6 om at eps = 1e-6 of the first-direction extraction vs chain; Richardson = |Q/chain - 1| of the eps -> 0 limits at om A; dR = |R^Q - R^chain|; slice = max componentwise relative error of the eps -> 0 slice):\n\n| branch | extracted | err (1e-6) | Richardson | tau_Q | R^Q | dR | slice err |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [6,2,0] | full (1 comp) | 0 (1e-131) | 0 | - | - | - | - |\n| [6,1,1] | full (1 comp), leading | 3.1e-7 | 9.9e-20 | - | - | - | - |\n| [5,3,0] | full (1 comp), leading | 2.1e-6 | 5.4e-20 | - | - | - | - |\n| [5,2,1] #1 | full: u'.C + R | 4.0e-6 | 1.1e-19 | 13.28200213 | -0.892188641588 | 6.2e-17 | 1.6e-16 |\n| [5,2,1] #2 | full: u'.C + R | 2.5e-6 | 1.5e-19 | 37.47881420 | 1.20406982971 | 2.6e-16 | 1.3e-15 |\n| [4,4,0] | full (1 comp), leading (kappa = (t+1)/2) | 9.5e-7 | 6.3e-19 | - | - | - | - |\n| [4,3,1] #1 | full: u'.C + R | 2.5e-6 | 9.6e-20 | 9.815049286 | -0.0932674374557 | 1.7e-10 | 1.8e-9 |\n| [4,3,1] #2 | full: u'.C + R | 1.7e-6 | 1.5e-19 | 35.63148133 | 0.547106166786 | 2.4e-10 | 7.4e-9 |\n| [4,2,2] | full: u'.C + R | 5.6e-7 | 1.2e-18 | - | -0.485875706215 | 1.9e-16 | 3.8e-16 |\n| [3,3,2] | full (1 comp), leading (eps^2 covector, kappa closed) | 2.7e-7 | 1.9e-19 | - | - | - | - |\n\n**P3 (out of sample: h = 1/2, theta = (3/7,-1/4), t = 19/14)**:\n\n| branch | extracted | err (1e-6) | Richardson | tau_Q | R^Q | dR | slice err |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [6,2,0] | full | 0 | 0 | - | - | - | - |\n| [6,1,1] | full, leading | 5.4e-7 | 2.8e-19 | - | - | - | - |\n| [5,3,0] | full, leading | 2.1e-6 | 4.2e-20 | - | - | - | - |\n| [5,2,1] #1 | full: u'.C + R | 3.8e-6 | 3.7e-19 | 5.660760026 | -0.685948111847 | 4.7e-17 | 2.5e-16 |\n| [5,2,1] #2 | full: u'.C + R | 4.7e-6 | 3.1e-19 | 26.85964814 | 1.29261477851 | 3.1e-17 | 1.0e-16 |\n| [4,4,0] | full, leading | 6.4e-7 | 4.4e-19 | - | - | - | - |\n| [4,3,1] #1 | full: u'.C + R | 1.8e-6 | 3.1e-19 | 4.006458515 | -0.0492541950103 | 1.6e-8 | 3.3e-7 |\n| [4,3,1] #2 | full: u'.C + R | 4.7e-6 | 3.6e-19 | 24.44252108 | 0.865785999106 | 2.3e-8 | 2.1e-7 |\n| [4,2,2] | full: u'.C + R | 2.4e-6 | 1.6e-18 | - | -0.373983739837 | 1.8e-17 | 5.0e-17 |\n| [3,3,2] | full, leading | 2.9e-6 | 9.5e-19 | - | - | - | - |\n\nReading: \"first direction only\" is never the limit: every branch is extracted completely (1-component weights from the leading formula with kappa(t); the dim-2 weights through R). The [4,3,1] second direction is limited to 1e-8 (P1: 1e-10) by the noise of the fitted alpha(t); the [4,2,2], [5,2,1] ones by nothing but the arithmetic (1e-16). The eps = 1e-6 errors are the expected O(eps) (leading-order formulas); the eps -> 0 Richardson limits agree to <= 1.6e-18.\n",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### [3,1,0] round 2 result\n\n**Task A (closed forms of the O(eps) constants, h = 1, theta = (t,0), 20 t, fit 14 / held-out 6):** kappa[4,4,0] = (t+1)/2 (2.6e-18); kappa[4,2,2] = (11t-31)/(5(3t-7)) (1.9e-17; pole at t = 7/3); kappa[3,3,2] = (t+1)(19t-49)/(40(t-2)) (4.9e-17); [4,3,1]: kappa_c = A + B tau_c with A = (-7t^4+26t^3-166t+75)/(9D), B = (7t^2-22t+23)/(36D), D = t^3+3t^2-17t+5 (held-out 9e-16); exact t2(theta1+h): tr/det on HW_[4,3,1] = 8t^2+16t-8, 16t(t-1)(t+1)(t+4); on HW_[5,2,1] 8t^2+19t-8, 4(t+4)(t-1)(t+1)(4t+3); t1(theta1+h) is degenerate on the [4,3,1] pair. [5,2,1]: R_c = 3/2 - 2t + tau_c/(2(t+4)) (1e-18), signal slopes p1' = (t-5)/4, q1' = (7-3t)/2, Delta_c = slope - p1' - q1' R_c = (111+44t-92t^2)/105 + (23t-13)/(105(t+4)) tau_c (1.6e-9, noise-limited; the coordinator's combination slope + (t-2)R is also affine in tau_c).\n\n**Task B (eps^2 layer):** exact covector with u' = (1,xU), u = (0,1); the coefficients a2/fac1, b2/fac1 are exactly linear in om2; g = F1/F0 is a straight line in om2, om1- and phi-independent in slope; R-coefficient = om2-slope of b2/fac1; the natural structural constant is kslope = kappa_0 x remainder slope: [4,2,2] rational in t (1.5e-11), [4,3,1] affine in tau_c with beta(t) rational (1.7e-11) and alpha(t) a degree-8/D^2 numerical fit (1e-9); R_c([4,3,1]) = A_R + B_R tau_c (D denominator), R[4,2,2] = -2(t-3)/(3(3t-7)). Not fitted: the remainder rem_c itself as affine-in-tau_c.\n\n**Task C (pure Q-side extraction, P1 and P3):** all 10 branches extracted completely; eps = 1e-6 errors <= 4.7e-6, Richardson agreement <= 1.6e-18, second directions: [5,2,1], [4,2,2] to 1e-16, [4,3,1] to 1.7e-10 (P1) / 2.3e-8 (P3).\n\n**Bug fixed:** `qtkC` memo not purged in `setPoint` (stale Q numbers across t); purge now literal-symbol including `qtkC`.\n",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
